SuperTools: prism overlap removal and sfdp's smoothing without the GTS library.

Graphviz builds these parts only with GTS (LGPL, on top of GLib), which no WebAssembly build has: sfdp then
reports "remove_overlap: Graphviz not built with triangulation library" for every drawing and leaves nodes
overlapping, and overlap=prism is refused. All they need from GTS is a Delaunay triangulation of the node positions.

lib/neatogen/delaunay.c gets a third branch (beside "GTS" and "nothing") that takes the triangulation from
st_delaunay.h — our C port of Delaunator, see that file — and the three places that ask "is GTS there?" before using
prism (overlap.c, adjust.c, sfdpinit.c) accept that branch too. lib/neatogen/neatosplines.c is left alone: its GTS
path (a spline router for parallel edges in the spring engines) needs a triangulation that keeps given segments,
which this is not.

--- a/lib/neatogen/delaunay.c
+++ b/lib/neatogen/delaunay.c
@@ -514,6 +514,92 @@
